      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IMPRESS SPIETH (7) hit the ground running from the squeeze draw with a slick early split, holding on for a minor placing when third and beaten 1.75 lengths at Gunnedah over 340m in 19.79. Comes out of a solid form race last start. Makes plenty of appeal. ZIPPING AUGUSTA (4) drew an outside box and was game in defeat when only 1.3 lengths from the winner Ancestral Queen in second(20.89) at this track. Likely to be in the finish again. NATURAL ESSENCE (2) is better than last start when sixth (25.64) from Box 3 at Goulburn over 440m. Form from her last run is proving to be solid. Shapes as one to consider. VINTAGE RACER (1) warrants respect although new to this track.",
